{%- comment -%}
  The USP trio, one component for all three places it appears (homepage proof
  band, PDP under the info sections, PDP buy column). Before this existed each
  surface printed its own bare <ul> of 10px grey text and every one of them read
  as filler.

  Icons are the thin line set from snippets/icon.liquid — shipping / dispatch
  time / secure payment, in that order, matched to the three lines by position.
  Copy stays a safe, verifiable fact: no guarantees, no invented delivery dates.

  Params: one / two / three (strings) · layout: 'trio' (default, 3 across) or
  'col' (stacked, for the narrow buy column).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign usp_layout = layout | default: 'trio' -%}
<ul class="usp usp--{{ usp_layout }}" aria-label="{{ 'usp.store_promises_aria' | t }}">
  {%- if one != blank -%}
    <li><span class="usp__ico" aria-hidden="true">{% render 'icon', name: 'truck', size: 20 %}</span><span class="lbl">{{ one | escape }}</span></li>
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if two != blank -%}
    <li><span class="usp__ico" aria-hidden="true">{% render 'icon', name: 'clock', size: 20 %}</span><span class="lbl">{{ two | escape }}</span></li>
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if three != blank -%}
    <li><span class="usp__ico" aria-hidden="true">{% render 'icon', name: 'lock', size: 20 %}</span><span class="lbl">{{ three | escape }}</span></li>
  {%- endif -%}
</ul>
